# Development API base URL for the mobile app.
#
# `localhost` is correct for the iOS simulator, which shares the host's network
# stack, and for Android — but Android needs help: inside an emulator (and on a
# USB-attached phone) `localhost` means the device itself, not this Mac. The
# bridge is `adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080`, applied by `make mb-reverse` once
# the device or emulator is up. (`make dev` opens iOS only; Android is manual.)
#
# The one case this value does NOT cover is a physical iPhone: there is no adb,
# so it must reach the Mac over the network. Point this at the machine's LAN IP
# (`ipconfig getifaddr en0`) for that session — the API already binds
# 0.0.0.0:8080, so it is reachable. The healthcheck screen prints whatever
# resolves here, so a wrong value is visible on first launch.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
